# WonderPress agent contract

This file is generated by `wonderpress agents write`. Do not hand-edit the
index below; it is rebuilt from `.wonderpress/manifest/`. The preamble is the
project-invariant contract.

## How to change a component

1. Edit `.wonderpress/manifest/partials/<slug>.json` (fields, types, labels).
2. Run `wonderpress partial sync <Name>` (or `--all`).
3. Put markup only in the PHP **view** (`partials/*.php`). Compose core Image
   and Link primitives instead of inventing `<img>` or new-tab `<a>` tags.

Do **not** hand-edit `src/partials/class-*.php` `$_properties` or
`blocks/<slug>/block.json` — they are generated and `partial sync` overwrites
them. Check with `wonderpress partial check-drift --all`.

## Markup rules

- The PHP partial view is the **only** source of HTML. Do not duplicate markup
  in JavaScript or JSX.
- Page lock is `'all'`, `'insert'`, or `false`. Never `contentOnly`.
- `--namespace` is committed once block content exists. Do not change it.
- Dual-authorable types (`image`, `link`, `post_object`, `repeater`, `partial`)
  share one value shape across ACF and the block editor. See
  `wonderpress-cli` docs: getting-started.md, manifest-first-partials.md,
  property-value-shapes.md.

## Commands

```
wonderpress partial list --format json
wonderpress partial create --json @spec.json
wonderpress partial add-js <Name>
wonderpress partial sync --all
wonderpress partial check-drift --all --format json
wonderpress lint --format json
wonderpress lint --fix
```

MCP `lint_theme` is the same inspect; pass `fix: true` for phpcbf (CLI `--fix`).
Drift is `partial_sync`, not `--fix`. `acf install` is not an MCP tool — run
`ACF_PRO_LICENSE=… wonderpress acf install` on the host CLI. Do not pass the
license as a flag or tool argument.

Machine-readable output: add `--format json` (envelope `{ ok, data, error }`).
Exit `0` success, `1` lint/drift/validation, `2` usage.

